# Rimefall Milestone 1.2: OSRS-style mechanical movement (from a real DualShock 4 playtest)

Playtest feedback on 1.1: "sometimes the speed will randomly slow down. it does feel like i get snagged on pillar corners. drifting into diagonals at times when it's not intentional. osrs is very mechanical and the speed is always the same."

Goal: movement must be perfectly regular, like OSRS. Make ONLY the changes below and output the COMPLETE contents of every file you change (=== FILE === format). Keep the module structure and all existing window.__rimefall fields (tileToScreen, meshScreen, meshWorld, hintText, lastMoveDir, player, tick, alpha, paused, inputDevice, isWalkable, blockers).

1. Camera faces north (the OSRS default). Set camera yaw so the camera sits due south of the player (+z side) looking north (-z): screen-up = grid north (-z), screen-right = grid east (+x). Keep the current pitch, distance, FOV and smooth follow. Now remove the camera-relative projection mapping: the stick and WASD map directly to grid directions (up/W = north (0,-1), right/D = east (1,0), etc.; two keys = diagonal). Remove the code that is no longer needed, keeping pickGridDir as a small pure function for the new snapping (rule 3).

2. Constant-speed rendering, with no tricks:
   - Remove the pre-glide/early-start and any easing, return-glide or catch-up logic, and any visual clock separate from the ticker.
   - The player mesh position = lerp(prevTile, currentTile, alpha), where alpha = (now - lastTickTime) / 600 clamped to [0,1], from the ticker. It's linear, so every tile (including diagonals) takes exactly one tick at constant speed. The step bob may stay but must use the same alpha, and it must not affect x/z.
   - Drift-free ticker (tick.js): use performance.now() with a fixed-step schedule. nextTickTime += 600 each tick (not "now + 600"), so jitter never accumulates. If more than 2 ticks behind (tab hidden, long stall), resync (nextTickTime = now + 600) instead of bursting multiple ticks. Also handle document visibilitychange (resync on becoming visible) and pause/resume (resync). Process at most 1 tick per frame normally (2 max when catching up by under 2 ticks). Expose lastTickTime for alpha.
   - Make sure input is polled in the same frame BEFORE the ticker fires, so the tick always sees the latest stick state.
   - Eliminate stop-then-restart: a tick with no direction must happen only when the player truly released the input.

3. Stick processing (input.js), evaluated every frame with persistent state; the tick uses the current "held direction":
   - Start deadzone 0.35 (radial). Release deadzone 0.25: if a direction is currently held and the magnitude stays >= 0.25, it stays held (hysteresis), even if it dips under 0.35.
   - Angle snapping: the 4 cardinal sectors are each 70° wide (±35° around N/E/S/W); diagonals only within ±10° of 45°/135°/225°/315°.
   - Direction hysteresis: once a direction is held, keep it until the stick angle goes more than 12° past that direction's sector boundary; then switch to the sector it is in.
   - Read the stick axes fresh every frame (axes 0/1, standard mapping, axis 1 positive = down/south).
   - Keyboard: unchanged semantics (W/A/S/D/arrows, two keys = diagonal). The most recently used device wins.
   - The D-pad (12-15) still must NOT move the player (it only queues gear swaps).

4. Corner rule with OSRS-like sliding (main.js tryMove): diagonals still can't cut corners. But if a diagonal move is blocked (the target tile is blocked, or either orthogonal neighbour is blocked), fall back to a free cardinal component instead of stopping: try the component with the larger stick magnitude first (for keyboard or a tie, try x/east-west first), then the other one; move if that tile is walkable. Facing follows the actual move made. lastMoveDir = the actual move made (or null).

5. Polish: the gamepad hint (#hint) should use the same styling as the keyboard hint: button/key names wrapped in <b> (yellow), separators in the same style. PlayStation: "<b>Left stick</b> move · <b>✕</b> attack · <b>□</b> eat · <b>D-pad</b> swap gear · <b>Options</b> pause"; Xbox the same with A / X / D-pad / Start.

6. index.html title: "Rimefall — Milestone 1.2".

7. Add a test hook: window.__rimefall.moveLog, an array (keep the last 200) of {tick, fromX, fromZ, toX, toZ} pushed on every tick (to = from when no move), and get lastTickTime.

